  <iati-identifier>47045-IND-C-SAATHII</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="47045" secondary-reporter="0" type="30">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribute to the national goals of ending AIDS by 2030, and TB elimination by 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">India - TB/HIV - Solidarity and Action Against The HIV Infection in India - SAATHII.  This program has the following goals: The goal of the project is to contribute to the national goal of ending AIDS by 2030. The program will support NACO&apos;s expansion of its new model for a comprehensive continuum of care from prevention to treatment..  To reduce morbidity and mortality due to TB and contribute to achieving National TB Program&apos;s goal of elimination by 2025. The objectives of this program are: Increase the proportion of prison inmates and those at OCS who know their HIV status from 56% to 100% in 10 states/UTs.  Increase the proportion of other vulnerable populations (spouses and family members, and partners of PLHIV) who know their HIV status from 43% to 73% in 10 states/UTs.  Increase the proportion of HIV-exposed infants who received the virological test within 6 months of birth from 92% to 100% in 10 states/Uts.  Increase the proportion of PLHIV LFU to ART Center tracked back with definite outcome from 50% to 98% in 10 states/UTs.  Increase the proportion of PLHIV due for VL test that have been tested for VL from 60% to 95%.  Increase the pediatric TB case notification in nine states from 59219 (2022) to 74170 (2026-27).  Increase the pediatric TB treatment success rate in nine states from 90% (2021) to 92% (2026-27).  Increase the annual TB case notification by 4564 in 60 districts of 8 states through deployment of portable handheld X-ray device as part of TB case finding activities.  Increase the annual TB case notification among the prisoners from 18 to 142 in 10 states and UTs by March 2027</narrative>
  </description>
